Day 39: Waiting with Hope | Saturday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“I wait for the Lord, my soul waits.”
Not passive.
Not empty.
Trust in motion.

Welcome to Day 39 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into the quiet, steady posture of waiting — not the restless kind that leaves you anxious, but the hopeful kind that anchors you in God’s faithfulness. Waiting with God is never wasted. It becomes prayer, trust, and expectation.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that God is working even when you cannot see it. His timing is wise. His heart is good. His promises are sure. Lent teaches you to wait with openness, with hope, and with confidence that the God you are waiting for is already near.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why waiting with God is active trust, not passive delay

How hope is anchored in God’s character, not circumstances

Why your waiting becomes prayer and steady faith

A prayer to trust God’s timing and faithfulness

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, I wait with You.”

